      "function": "explanation",
      "scene_type": "gritwerk_paper",
      "duration_hint": 18,
      "spoken": "The psychologist Peter Gollwitzer describes these plans like this: if situation x happens, then I will do y. The plan links an expected moment to an action ahead of time. It does not replace your goal. It attaches to a goal you already have.",
      "data": {
        "headline": "The if-then plan",
        "tag": "Journal article",
        "cite": "Gollwitzer 1999",
        "claim": "If situation x happens, then I will do y.",
